From 874a01bae400655f32c717bd67d0c6e376db97d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 01:38:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02714/11362] [outer-loop] Unblock .409 activation: drop
 literal mmcblk token from exp4428 KV260 precondition

The .409 activation guard HARD-blocked 5x consecutively (WRONG_MECHANISM_PRECONDITION): the
exclusion-manifest linter naive-substring-matches the retired host-SD-card device path against
any prompt that also references the KV260/kria board -- and my exp4428 prompt contained that
literal token inside a NEGATION ("NEVER <that path> -- host SD slot is retired"). The linter
cannot tell the negation from a real precondition, so the guard-rail wording tripped the guard.
Rephrased to convey SSH-reachability-only + retired-mechanism-forbidden without the literal
token. Intent unchanged; YAML parses; conductor's next retry can now activate .409.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 research-roadmap-next.yaml | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/research-roadmap-next.yaml b/research-roadmap-next.yaml
index 8bce2bfc39..947da89751 100644
--- a/research-roadmap-next.yaml
+++ b/research-roadmap-next.yaml
@@ -239,8 +239,9 @@ tasks:
     deliverable: results/experiment_4428_hardware_continuity.json
     prompt: |
       One forward step (or documentation/audit if blocked on operator action) per attached board. KV260:
-      PRECONDITION ssh -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o BatchMode=yes kria 'true' (NEVER /dev/mmcblk -- host SD slot
-      is retired); if unreachable, honest_verdict blocked_kv260_ssh_unreachable. GateMate: nextpnr-himbaechel
+      PRECONDITION ssh -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o BatchMode=yes kria 'true' (SSH-reachability is the ONLY valid
+      KV260 precondition; the retired host SD-card-device mechanism is forbidden per KV260 SSH-Not-SD-Card
+      Discipline); if unreachable, honest_verdict blocked_kv260_ssh_unreachable. GateMate: nextpnr-himbaechel
       (NOT nextpnr-gatemate) + openFPGALoader -c dirtyJtag --detect. PolarFire: ssh polarfire 'true'. For
       each reachable board take the next concrete step (latency transcript / bitstream pack / sampler smoke
       per its track); for each blocked board emit a precondition-gated blocked_<resource> + a one-line
